{
  "description": "Cross-tier timing: the COMPLETE LOGOS CPU (integer + div/mod + collections + recursion + functions + IEEE-754 float + float-heap + Text + Word32/crypto) running the WHOLE 35-benchmark suite on a real Nexys A7-100T (Artix-7 xc7a100t) via the open FOSS flow (yosys+nextpnr+prjxray, no Vivado). FOUR TIERS, same program each: host_interp_ns = the tree-walking interpreter; host_vm_ns = the register-bytecode VM (run_nanos, min-of-3000, SAME bytecode the chip runs); host_aot_native_ns = LOGOS->Rust->rustc -O3 -C target-cpu=native, run-only min-of-N in-process (NOTE: rustc constant-folds fixed-input programs, so this is a LOWER BOUND \u2014 the compiled tier is at least this fast; loop/LCG-data benchmarks like bubble_sort/mandelbrot/quicksort show real compute, the tiny arithmetic ones fold to ~ns). chip = the on-chip hardware cycle counter (run-only). chip_ns_at_6p25mhz = the divided core clock the bitstream ships (open-flow routing margin); chip_ns_at_fmax = the routed worst-case corner. interp_over_vm_speedup = host tree-walk / bytecode. cycle_efficiency_vs_host_vm = host clocks / chip cycles for the same work (the native datapath's per-clock advantage). Every silicon Show output is BIT-EXACT to the VM (35/35).",
